  "interpretation": "Full Std and Init workflows can exceed the unchanged memory limit. Initial-goal checks missed later proof and package work. Explicit single-threaded and synchronous Lean checks did not materially reduce the saved bad draft\u2019s memory. Importing only Nat.Gcd reduces the isolated checker cost, but the package entry also needs prelude to avoid implicitly loading Init. Changing both headers preserves the executable and claims and completes the same native workflow at 517160960 sampled bytes. These are controlled no-model checks, not agent outcomes or an fr-versus-ordinary-tools overhead comparison. Require the full automated workflow and 128 MiB of client-state headroom before any fresh calls.",
  "invalid_control": "The first combined control used the Docker fixture directory /workspace and was denied before fr ran. It is retained as invalid setup; the corrected-directory control reached the memory limit.",
  "publication": "Reviewed numeric summaries and hashes only; raw traces remain local.",
